TY  - JOUR
AU  - Chen, Wei
AU  - Smith, Sarah
AU  - Tanaka, Yuki
TI  - Spatial transcriptomics reveals tumor microenvironment heterogeneity in colorectal cancer
JO  - Nature Medicine
PY  - 2023
VL  - 29
IS  - 4
SP  - 812
EP  - 825
DO  - 10.1038/s41591-023-02345-6
AB  - Spatial transcriptomics enables the mapping of gene expression within intact tissue sections. We applied spatial transcriptomics to 45 colorectal cancer specimens and identified distinct tumor microenvironment niches associated with patient outcomes. Our analysis revealed spatially restricted immune cell populations and their interactions with cancer cells.
ER  -

TY  - CONF
AU  - Patel, Priya
AU  - Mueller, Anna
AU  - Garcia, Maria
TI  - Machine learning approaches for biomarker discovery in spatially resolved transcriptomic data
JO  - Proceedings of the International Conference on Bioinformatics
PY  - 2022
SP  - 134
EP  - 142
DO  - 10.1145/3535508.3545539
AB  - We developed a graph neural network framework for identifying spatially variable genes and biomarkers from spatial transcriptomics data. Applied to colorectal cancer tissue microarrays, our method identified 23 novel biomarker candidates with improved predictive accuracy compared to conventional differential expression analysis.
ER  -

TY  - BOOK
AU  - Zhang, Wei
AU  - Johnson, James
AU  - Andersson, Lars
TI  - Atlas of Spatial Omics in Colorectal Cancer
PB  - Springer Nature
PY  - 2024
DO  - 10.1007/978-3-031-45678-9
AB  - This comprehensive atlas provides a detailed reference for spatial omics technologies applied to colorectal cancer research. Covering spatial transcriptomics, spatial proteomics, and spatial metabolomics, the book presents standardized protocols, computational pipelines, and clinical applications for understanding tumor heterogeneity.
